codex
The corrected evidence still supports sending population 2 back to the owner: initialization contains direct accesses with no local probe or recovery wrapper. It does not prove inevitable guest termination. The guest assembly reads DPFSR from the CMMU, and returning zero for IRQSTAT would make an invoked abort handler skip its clear and NMI handling.
codex
VERDICT: CONFIRM WITH CHANGES (7)

**1 | Seven factual corrections or qualifications:**

1. **“six unconditional, non-probe, word-width accesses.”** There are **six registers and seven access sites**: five initialization operations across MASTERCTL, MASTER3, MASTER4 and MASTER4MOD; two abort-handler operations. Initialization is straight-line once the enabled VME2 branch runs. IRQSTAT is read when the handler runs; IRQCLR is written **only if the abort-status bit is set**. None has a local probe/recovery wrapper. The cited guest-header field widths were outside the permitted reading. See [initialization](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_guest-src-openbsd22/sys/arch/mvme88k/dev/vme.c:443) and [abort handler](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_guest-src-openbsd22/sys/arch/mvme88k/dev/vme.c:570).

2. **“has ALREADY matched (on offset 0, served).”** False for this guest: `vmematch()` checks attachment information and returns without accessing any VME register. The attribution of the emulator’s probing comment to “some later OpenBSD” is unsupported by the inspected sources. See [vmematch](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_guest-src-openbsd22/sys/arch/mvme88k/dev/vme.c:73).

3. **“models no DPFSR at all”** and **“would instead end the GUEST at the same instruction.”** The first inference is unsupported; the second is conditional, not established. Guest assembly obtains DPFSR through a **memory-mapped CMMU status read**, so absence of a `dpfsr` token in CPU sources cannot settle its emulated value. The cited trap path supports recovery and calls `panictrap()` at its unresolved-fault tail only when `pcb_onfault` is zero. Actual exception state and boot reachability remain unmeasured. See [CMMU reads](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_guest-src-openbsd22/sys/arch/mvme88k/mvme88k/eh.S:1009) and [fault handling](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_guest-src-openbsd22/sys/arch/mvme88k/mvme88k/trap.c:292).

4. **“the file’s own sibling idiom (DECLINE + latched announce…).”** The **latched** part is false as a description of this file. Five existing cases call `debug()` on each applicable access; there is no announcement-latch state. Latching is a proposed addition or externally cited precedent. See [device state and cases](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:52).

5. **“40 … sub-word starts.”** The arithmetic is correct, but the unit needs precision: **40 width/address combinations at 30 distinct offsets**—30 byte accesses plus 10 aligned halfword accesses. Sixteen combinations concern the four storing words; 24 concern the six other cased words. CPU-path reachability was not independently checked because the CPU sources are excluded.

6. **“per-chapter page-footer census … 7: 12; 8: 38; 9: 9.”** These reproduce regex matches, **not chapter page counts**. The [PDF](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/vmesbcp2.pdf) contains:

   | Contents | Physical pages | Count |
   |---|---:|---:|
   | Front matter | 1–24 | 24 |
   | Chapter 5 | 25–94 | 70 |
   | Chapter 6 | 95–146 | 52 |
   | Chapter 7 | 147–160 | 14 |
   | Chapter 8 | 161–200 | 40 |
   | Chapter 9 | 201–224 | 24 |
   | Index | 225–240 | 16 |

   **240 PDF pages and 240 text form feeds are confirmed. Chapter 4 is absent from the body.** The chapter-4 regex match is an index continuation. “Only 6 near-empty pages” depends on an unstated threshold and alone does not prove absence; the complete page inventory does. The cover explicitly says [“Part 2 of 2”](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/vmesbcp2.txt:4), identifying `VMESBCA2/PG1`. This establishes absence from the inspected volume, not absence everywhere “on disk” or accidental truncation.

7. **ELSE #1: “lane-wrong, silently” / “No kill, no announce,”** and the asserted guest doubleword behavior. The blanket description is too broad: five cased arms call `debug()`, and only four store backing words. The concrete VBR byte defects are supported. A single length-eight callback would truncate a storing assignment, but these permitted files do **not** establish that a guest doubleword instruction reaches it as one such callback. See [device dispatch](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:68).

The other requested checks pass:

- **26 named-but-unhandled registers:** 36 header-defined register offsets minus ten cases.
- **Containing-word shortcut:** on big-endian reads it returns the low byte/halfword, ignoring the requested lane. Consequently byte lanes +1/+2 are wrong; +3 happens to agree, as does halfword +2. Sub-word writes to storing cases replace the entire backing word. [Helpers](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/memory.c:55).
- **T1COUNT side effect:** reads increment backing state by 100 and return the **pre-increment** snapshot. Interior accesses trigger this only under the hypothetical rounded dispatch; currently they reach `default:`. [T1COUNT](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:90).
- **Unchanged since import:** the sole file-history commit is `39748e3c`, dated 2026-06-28; the current working-tree content matches its imported blob.

**2 | Yes.** The five direct initialization operations remain evidence of ordinary driver traffic outside a local probe/recovery wrapper. That supports returning population 2 to the owner with corrected facts. It does not establish inevitable guest panic or independently select the pending disposition.

**3 | The owner needs the initialization and abort consequences separated, and the actual CMMU/exception state established before treating guest termination as certain.** Registration of the abort handler does not establish its invocation; guest configuration and field-width claims also remain outside this check.

**ELSE found:** serving IRQSTAT as zero has a concrete consequence omitted from the ruling: an invoked abort handler returns zero before clearing the interrupt or calling `nmihand()`. Thus the proposed zero-read behavior also needs an explicit consequence statement. [Abort branch](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_guest-src-openbsd22/sys/arch/mvme88k/dev/vme.c:576).

Read-only throughout; nothing written or built. Excluded artifacts and ledger claims were not independently checked.
